The YAML confirms that `securityContext.runAsNonRoot: true` is *already* set in the Pod spec, which is what triggered the error in the first place.

```yaml
  securityContext:
    runAsNonRoot: true
```

The error message from the Kubelet was:
`Warning Failed 15s (x4 over 43s) kubelet spec.containers{app}: Error: container has runAsNonRoot and image will run as root (pod: "app-56c6cdc6d6-c6l8x_default(3cde7d86-cea9-47de-b73d-db3057c6920e)", container: app)`

Since the Pod definition requires non-root execution (`runAsNonRoot: true`), and the image (`busybox:1.37.0`) is running as root, the fix is to explicitly tell the container to run as a non-root user using `runAsUser`.

I need to patch the Pod to add `runAsUser: 1000` (or another non-root UID) under `spec.containers[0].securityContext`.

I will use a JSON merge patch this time, as it is often more reliable for targeted additions/modifications within a structure than strategic merge patch when dealing with lists/sub-objects.

The patch structure for JSON merge patch:
```json
{
  "spec": {
    "containers": [
      {
        "name": "app",
        "securityContext": {
          "runAsUser": 1000
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```
Note: `runAsNonRoot` is already true, so I only need to add the UID.

I will attempt this patch.

The owner of the ReplicaSet `app-56c6cdc6d6` is a Deployment named `app`.

The faulty state is owned by the Deployment `app` in the `default` namespace. I must now patch this Deployment.

The patch needs to add `securityContext: {runAsNonRoot: true, runAsUser: 1000}` to the container definition within the Deployment's Pod template.

I will use a strategic merge patch on the Deployment.

Patch target:
```json
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "securityContext": {
              "runAsNonRoot": true,
              "runAsUser": 1000
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```
This structure assumes the deployment template has a container named "app". The Pod description confirmed this: `containers.name: app`.

I will execute the patch.

